{
  "_comment": "The ten-lane interest map from 'GitHub Repo Discovery Strategy'. Edit this file, commit, and the next run picks it up. Date macros {d-N} expand to today minus N days, so queries never go stale.",
  "settings": {
    "results_per_query": 30,
    "max_candidates_per_lane": 6,
    "max_candidates_total": 24,
    "min_score": 1.5,
    "min_age_days": 14,
    "velocity_cap": 2.5,
    "_guard_note": "min_age_days keeps day-old repos out until they have a little history; velocity_cap stops one implausible star spike from owning every run.",
    "guaranteed_per_lane": 2,
    "_min_score_note": "Raised from 0.25 after the first live run let a cloud-certification study repo into lane 4 purely to satisfy the per-lane coverage guarantee. A guaranteed slot should stay empty rather than be filled with noise.",
    "weak_min_score": 2.5,
    "_weak_min_score_note": "Floor for repos matched only by a lane keyword in the name or description, with no topic tag and no followed org. Lanes share vocabulary deliberately ('transcription' is both journalism and video), so a keyword-only hit is a collision until proved otherwise. No pick in the 2026-09-06 all-lane run was weak-only, so this costs nothing there and cleans up the thin single-lane runs.",
    "require_english": true,
    "english_min_share": 0.6,
    "english_check_limit": 25,
    "_english_note": "A repo whose description is mostly non-Latin script is dropped unless it ships an English README in its root (README.en.md and friends), which means the translation already exists. english_min_share is the share of letters that must be Latin; english_check_limit caps how many root listings one run will fetch looking for a translation.",
    "_velocity_cap_note": "Lowered from 4.0 (10,000 stars/month) to 2.5 (~316/month) on 2026-09-06. At 4.0 every viral general-audience repo pinned the cap, so lane weights and crossovers never got to decide anything: the first live all-lane run gave lane 1 six repos with 28k-125k stars and none of them about agent design."
  },
  "velocity_query": {
    "_comment": "Lane-agnostic. Young and already popular: catches repos that will reach a lane next month.",
    "query": "stars:>500 created:>{d-60} archived:false",
    "enabled": true
  },
  "crossovers": {
    "_comment": "Multiplier when a repo matches both lanes. 1+9 is the rarest skill overlap; 1+10 is the most immediately practical.",
    "1+9": 1.6,
    "1+10": 1.4,
    "8+9": 1.3,
    "1+2": 1.3,
    "8+10": 1.25
  },
  "global_excludes": {
    "_comment": "Hard excludes, not soft penalties. These are the repos that pollute topic searches: interview prep, roadmaps, course lists, cheat sheets. Learned from the single-region penalty in research-digest-dashboard, where a soft score never actually kept junk out.",
    "name_or_description": "(?i)(interview[ -](questions|prep|guide)|cracking[ -]the|\\broadmap\\b|cheat[ -]?sheet|100[ -]days|free[ -]?(courses?|books?)|学习路线|面试|^awesome[ -]|\\bawesome[ -](list|collection)|curated (list|collection) of|\\d{2,}\\+? (tools|resources|projects)\\b|a[- ]shares?\\b|\\bstock (trading|market|picking)|quantitative[- ]trading|\\bbacktest|trading[- ]bot|\\bcrypto[- ]?(bot|trading)|portfolio[- ]optimi)",
    "_finance_note": "Added 2026-09-06. Nothing in the ten lanes is about equities or trading, but investing workbenches tag themselves mcp/ai-agents/research-assistant/nextjs and so stack four strong lanes. On the first live all-lane run a China A-shares research terminal scored 10.3, the highest of any repo in any lane. Deliberately narrow: it names trading instruments and strategies, not 'finance', so that financial-accountability reporting tools in lanes 8 and 9 still come through."
  },
